---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CTAStrip from '../components/CTAStrip.astro';

const bookingUrl = 'https://calendar.app.google/hH5ewNekVCHFKrcc9';
---

<Base>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <h1 class="hero-headline">Every call answered. Every lead captured. Even when you can't pick up.</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">Most small businesses lose more work to missed calls than to anything else &mdash; and they never see it happen. Standard Method Group sets up call coverage that answers on the first ring, handles the routine questions, books the meeting, and sends you a clean message for anything that needs you.</p>
      <div class="hero-ctas">
        <a href={bookingUrl} class="hero-cta">Book a 30-minute call</a>
        <a href="/how-we-work" class="hero-cta-secondary">See how it works &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What it is — honest disclosure, plain body copy near the top -->
  <section class="disclosure">
    <div class="disclosure-inner">
      <p>It's not a person sitting by the phone &mdash; it's a voice system we set up and tune for your business. It answers the way you'd want it answered, handles the questions you get all day, and knows when to reach you. It works nights, weekends, and the moments you can't pick up.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What it does -->
  <section class="capabilities">
    <div class="capabilities-inner">
      <h2>What it does</h2>
      <ul class="capability-list">
        <li>Answers every call &mdash; first ring, every time, including nights and weekends.</li>
        <li>Handles the questions you answer fifty times a week &mdash; hours, location, what you do, whether you cover their area.</li>
        <li>Books the meeting straight onto your calendar, so a good lead becomes an appointment instead of a callback you'll forget.</li>
        <li>Captures the details &mdash; name, number, what they need &mdash; and sends them to you the moment the call ends.</li>
        <li>Knows when to reach you. Anything urgent comes straight through; everything else waits in a tidy summary.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Outbound -->
  <section class="outbound">
    <div class="outbound-inner">
      <h2>And it works the other direction, too.</h2>
      <p>When you've got leads sitting in a list going cold, the same setup can reach back out &mdash; following up on the people who already raised their hand, so the warm ones actually turn into conversations instead of going stale.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Bridge to deeper work -->
  <section class="bridge">
    <div class="bridge-inner">
      <h2>The phone is one piece.</h2>
      <p>Once your calls are handled, the same gaps usually show up elsewhere &mdash; the intake that gets re-typed three times, the follow-up that depends on someone remembering, the report that takes a day to pull. Call coverage is one of the simplest places to start. Most of what we build for clients lives in the spaces around it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Proof -->
  <section class="proof">
    <div class="proof-inner">
      <p>SMG client Edge Marine Construction had overdue invoices paid within the first month &mdash; not because someone chased them, but because the follow-up happened on its own. Call coverage is the same idea, applied to the conversations that start the work.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTAStrip
    headline="Want to hear what this would sound like for your business?"
    buttonText="Book a 30-minute call"
    buttonHref={bookingUrl}
  />
</Base>

<style>
  /* Hero */
  .hero {
    background: var(--color-warm-white);
    padding: var(--space-12) 0;
    min-height: 80vh;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .hero-inner {
    max-width: var(--max-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--space-3);
    max-width: 60%;
  }

  .hero-headline {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-heading);
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    color: var(--color-navy);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .hero-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .hero-ctas {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .hero-cta {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-heading);
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-white);
    background: var(--color-teal);
    padding: 14px 28px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background 200ms ease;
  }

  .hero-cta:hover {
    background: var(--color-deep-teal);
    color: var(--color-white);
  }

  .hero-cta:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid rgba(42, 125, 110, 0.4);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .hero-cta-secondary {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-heading-medium);
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-teal);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .hero-cta-secondary:hover {
    color: var(--color-deep-teal);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* Disclosure */
  .disclosure {
    background: var(--color-warm-white-alt);
    padding: var(--space-8) 0;
  }

  .disclosure-inner {
    max-width: var(--max-width-narrow);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--space-3);
  }

  .disclosure-inner p {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* Capabilities */
  .capabilities {
    padding: var(--space-12) 0;
  }

  .capabilities-inner {
    max-width: var(--max-width-narrow);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--space-3);
  }

  .capabilities h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-heading);
    font-size: 2rem;
    color: var(--color-navy);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .capability-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .capability-list li {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    line-height: 1.6;
    padding-left: var(--space-3);
    position: relative;
  }

  .capability-list li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.75em;
    width: 8px;
    height: 2px;
    background: var(--color-teal);
  }

  /* Outbound */
  .outbound {
    background: var(--color-warm-white);
    padding: var(--space-8) 0;
  }

  .outbound-inner {
    max-width: var(--max-width-narrow);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--space-3);
  }

  .outbound h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-heading);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--color-navy);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .outbound p {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* Bridge */
  .bridge {
    padding: var(--space-12) 0;
  }

  .bridge-inner {
    max-width: var(--max-width-narrow);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--space-3);
  }

  .bridge h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-heading);
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    color: var(--color-navy);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .bridge p {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* Proof */
  .proof {
    background: var(--color-warm-white-alt);
    padding: var(--space-8) 0;
  }

  .proof-inner {
    max-width: var(--max-width-narrow);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--space-3);
  }

  .proof-inner p {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* Mobile */
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .hero {
      min-height: auto;
      padding: var(--space-8) 0;
    }

    .hero-inner {
      max-width: 100%;
    }

    .hero-headline {
      font-size: 1.75rem;
    }

    .hero-sub {
      font-size: 1.125rem;
    }

    .disclosure,
    .capabilities,
    .outbound,
    .bridge,
    .proof {
      padding: var(--space-5) 0;
    }

    .disclosure-inner p {
      font-size: 1.125rem;
    }

    .capabilities h2 {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .bridge h2 {
      font-size: 1.375rem;
    }

    .outbound h2 {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
    }

    .capability-list li,
    .outbound p,
    .bridge p,
    .proof-inner p {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .hero-cta {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
